00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:07,680
Let's learn stick. As a noun. It means something\h
that's long, thin and often made of wood like\h\h

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:14,960
this. As a verb, it often means to attach\h
something to something else so that it can't move.\h\h

3
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:21,600
You need some glue to stick that on. Get some tape\h
to stick them together. Now, it's not just things;\h\h

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:26,920
an idea or a piece of information can stick\h
in your head. I'm going to keep studying this\h\h

5
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:34,120
until it sticks. Catchy songs always stick in\h
my head. We can use it figuratively to mean\h\h

6
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:40,440
to not change. We've made a decision and\h
we're going to stick with it. It's hard,\h\h

7
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:46,680
but I'm going to stick with this diet. We can also\h
use it as an informal alternative to put. Look,\h\h

8
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:53,040
it's in the way. Can you stick it somewhere else.\h
So, stick can be a piece of wood be a bit like\h\h

9
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:59,920
put, mean to stop something moving, or to not\h
change. Stick with us. And you'll keep learning.

10
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:07,960
Let's take a minute to look at some of the many\h
meanings 'while' can have. As a conjunction,\h\h

11
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:13,680
'while' can mean 'at the same\h
time as'. While we were sleeping,\h\h

12
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:22,280
it snowed! We can swap the two clauses around,\h
but notice the comma goes away. It snowed while\h\h

13
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:30,000
we were sleeping! 'While' can have the same\h
meaning as 'but'. One of the twins is shy,\h\h

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,160
while the other is outgoing. And 'while', or\h
'whilst' in more formal contexts, can also\h\h

15
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:43,680
be used in the same way as 'although'.\h
While I know that sugar is bad for me,\h\h

16
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:51,680
I can never say no to dessert! As a noun, 'while'\h
can mean 'a length of time' and, in the expression\h\h

17
00:01:51,680 --> 00:02:00,000
'worth your while', it can mean 'worth the\h
time and effort used'. So, finally... Even\h\h

18
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,320
though we only had a short while together,\h
we hope this lesson was worth your while.

19
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:13,680
Accept is a regular verb. Now let's look at\h
five different meanings it can have. Number one:\h\h

20
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:20,760
'accept' can mean 'to agree to take something\h
or receive something willingly'. This can be\h\h

21
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:29,040
anything from a gift, an award, an apology,\h
responsibility for something or even a form of\h\h

22
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:37,440
payment. Many shops don't accept cash anymore.\h
Number two: 'to say yes to an invitation or an\h\h

23
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:44,760
offer'. She accepted the job straight away! Number\h
three: 'to believe or recognise that something is\h\h

24
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:52,720
true'. The relationship has been over for weeks,\h
but he still refuses to accept it. Number four:\h\h

25
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:59,080
'to consider satisfactory or to give\h
approval'. Tommy was immediately accepted\h\h

26
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:05,920
by the other children at his new school. And\h
number five: 'to endure something without\h\h

27
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:13,720
complaint'. Even though it makes me sad, I\h
accept that my one minute with you is up.

28
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:20,280
Let's learn 'thought'. It's not just the past form\h
of the verb 'think', it's also a noun, and this is\h\h

29
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:27,160
where it gets interesting. Unsurprisingly, it's\h
all to do with things in our head. As a countable\h\h

30
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:34,120
noun, a thought can be an idea or a plan. I've\h
just had a thought! We should go to the beach.\h\h

31
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:41,560
There's a thought! Let's order pizza. As a plural\h
noun, it can refer to our opinions or beliefs.\h\h

32
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:47,200
Here are my thoughts on how to run a business.\h
What are your thoughts on the right age to give\h\h

33
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:54,120
a child a phone? As an uncountable noun, it can\h
refer to considering something carefully. This\h\h

34
00:03:54,120 --> 00:04:01,120
is a difficult problem we need to give it some\h
thought. Sorry, this just doesn't work it needs\h\h

35
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:09,360
more thought. Thoughts happen in your brain. They\h
can be ideas, opinions or beliefs. We also use it\h\h

36
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:15,880
to refer to considering a problem. It's easy to\h
remember. You just have to give it some thought.

37
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:22,360
Let's learn 'current'. As an adjective,\h
'current' relates to time. It means 'related\h\h

38
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:29,880
to the present', 'relevant now' or 'up to date'.\h
We need to reflect current trends. This is our\h\h

39
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:36,280
current plan, but it might change. As a\h
noun, 'current' describes steady continual\h\h

40
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:41,680
movement. We often use it with water,\h
air and electricity. Don't swim there.\h\h

41
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:48,120
The current is too strong. Pilots have to\h
learn about air currents. The electrical\h\h

42
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:53,960
current flows around the circuit. Another way\h
that current is used as a noun is to refer to\h\h

43
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:59,880
feelings and opinion when they're held by a lot\h
of people together. These writers all reflect the\h\h

44
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:05,600
same current of thought. As the band stepped\h
onto the stage, a current of excitement went\h\h

45
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:11,200
through the crowd. So current is all\h
about movement - whether that's time\h\h

46
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:19,680
water air electricity or feelings. Stay with\h
us we'll make sure your English stays current.

47
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:25,800
The word 'career' is most commonly used as a\h
noun to mean the job or jobs you do in your\h\h

48
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:33,440
working life, especially if you progress and earn\h
more money. I'm studying medicine because I want\h\h

49
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:42,120
a career as a doctor. She's had a very successful\h
career – she deserves an enjoyable retirement! We\h\h

50
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:49,840
can also use 'career' as an adjective before some\h
nouns, like 'development' and 'advice'. You must\h\h

51
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:55,960
take this training course as part of your career\h
development. I went to the HR department for\h\h

52
00:05:55,960 --> 00:06:03,800
career advice. We can also use 'career' as a verb\h
to describe something on wheels, like transport,\h\h

53
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:10,840
that moves fast and in an uncontrolled way.\h
The car careered off the road but, luckily,\h\h

54
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:18,440
the driver wasn't hurt. That bus is careering\h
towards that tree! It's lost control! So,\h\h

55
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:23,320
you can have a 'career' in something, like,\h
medicine, get some help with your 'career'\h\h

56
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:30,040
with career development or advice, and\h
transport can career out of control.

57
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:36,880
As an adjective, we use 'content' to mean\h
feeling happy and at peace with a situation.\h\h

58
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:43,360
I felt content sitting by the fire, watching\h
the rain outside. It can also mean you accept\h\h

59
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:51,400
something that is out of your control. She was\h
content with coming third in the race. As a noun,\h\h

60
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:57,840
'content' means the ideas or information\h
contained in something. I'm subscribed to\h\h

61
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:04,280
her money-saving channel because the content\h
is so interesting. Your writing is enjoyable\h\h

62
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:11,840
but it lacks content – add more detail please.\h
We can also use 'content' to talk about the high\h\h

63
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:20,360
or low amount of something contained in food\h
and drink. Soya milk has a low fat content.\h\h

64
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:27,000
This chocolate bar has a high sugar content.\h
We hope the content of this video makes you\h\h

65
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:33,800
feel more content with your English! And\h
if you enjoy our content, like this video!

66
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:41,800
Let's learn 'individual'. It can be a noun or an\h
adjective. As a noun it means a person. We used\h\h

67
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:47,680
the word 'individual' because we want to compare\h
a person to a group, while the person is a bit\h\h

68
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:53,680
different to everyone else. 'Almost everyone\h
passed. There's just one individual who let\h\h

69
00:07:53,680 --> 00:08:01,480
us down.' 'She's quite an individual. She has her\h
own style.' 'Individual' used as an adjective can\h\h

70
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:09,360
mean 'distinctive' or 'different'. 'Your taste is\h
very individual. I never know what you're like.'\h\h

71
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:16,160
'Individual' as an adjective can also describe\h
things that relate to each person within a group.\h\h

72
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:23,680
'We make sure that we deal with your individual\h
needs.' So, the word 'individual' is all about\h\h

73
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:29,840
things that relate to a single person and maybe\h
they're different or maybe we just want to look\h\h

74
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:37,240
at them differently. Whatever your interest as\h
an individual, we can help you learn English.

75
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:44,600
Let's learn course. A course, often has a\h
beginning and an end. If you set or follow a\h\h

76
